# expect: E304
# Derived from CatalaLang/catala tests/exception/good/exceptions_squared.catala_en
# Copyright (c) Inria and the Catala contributors. Apache-2.0.
# Modified: re-expressed in Payment Charter DSL.
#
# Catala's canonical priority test: x = 0, an exception giving 1, and an
# exception to that exception giving 2. It answers 2, by declared priority.
#
# Charter answers E304. S4 forces exceptions to be provably disjoint rather
# than resolving them by priority, so a chain of three conditions that all hold
# for the same request is rejected naming them. This is the deliberate
# divergence design.md records: we borrowed Catala's default-logic model and
# are stricter about ambiguity.
#
# The reason is that a ceiling resolved by priority is a ceiling a reviewer has
# to simulate. Under S4 every request meets exactly one value, and which one is
# readable without running anything.
charter exceptions-squared version 1
resolver common@41
timezone UTC

  asset USDC_circle = mint://USDC/Circle/EPjFWdd5AufqSSqeM2qN1xzybapC8G4wEGGkZwyTDt1v/solana:5eykt4UsFv8P8NJdTREpY1vzqKqZKvdp

  group everyone = { 7xKXtg2CW87d97TXJSDpbD5jBkheTqA83TZRuJosgAsU }

  limit x
    amount 0 USDC_circle
      except 100.00 USDC_circle when counterparty in everyone
      except 200.00 USDC_circle when counterparty in everyone
    per fixed day
